Z||000040||AkursedX||08-10-2000||01:42 AM||||Well my absolute favorite car is the DeTomaso Pantera.  Preferably a 1975 GTS5 *drool*  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I know it's an odd choice, but I love the style of it and I've seen some goregeous examples of it.  Plus they are mid-engined, just like my 2nd favorite car, hehe.<P>I think it should get a little bit more respect and recognition among the super-car world, but in a way it's good, because it makes them much cheaper to buy, so maybe I can own my dream car one day.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Heres a link to a bunch of awesome Pantera pics for those who don't know what it looks like (I don't know how to post pics)  <A HREF="http://www.panteracars.com/gallery1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.panteracars.com/gallery1.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by AkursedX (edited 08-10-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000041||Patrick||08-10-2000||04:05 PM||||<BR>AkursedX, you have excellent taste in cars!!! <P>I've always loved the Pantera. Whenever I see one at the car shows here, I can't help but stop and stare. How can the combination of Italian styling and American V8 horsepower be beat?!!! And as you've pointed out, a mid-engine design to boot. The only drawback is that it's Ford powered. This is the only reason I haven't bought one. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Seriously though, I wonder if anyone's ever put small or big block Chevy in a Pantera?||||reg||14
Z||000042||AkursedX||08-10-2000||05:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, lucidatypewriter">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Patrick:<BR><B><BR>Seriously though, I wonder if anyone's ever put small or big block Chevy in a Pantera?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I've seen a Pantera with a 426 hemi in it.  He had the dyno slip and it topped out at 503 horses at the rear wheels.  I've seen a Pantera for sale that had a small block chevy in it as well.  You can fit quite a few different engines into that cradle.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000043||Patrick||08-10-2000||05:53 PM||||<BR>I guess it was a silly question by me. After all, what kind of vehicle <I>hasn't</I> had a small or big block Chevy put into it at some point by someone?<P>Now if I could just find a Pantera here on the west coast that's had the conversion done and the price was right... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000044||AkursedX||08-11-2000||01:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, lucidatypewriter">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Patrick:<BR><B><P><BR>Now if I could just find a Pantera here on the west coast that's had the conversion done and the price was right...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You would be suprised how many Panteras pop up for sale.  Every now and then just take a look at <A HREF="http://www.autotrader.com" TARGET=_blank>www.autotrader.com</A>   or <A HREF="http://www.ebaymotors.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ebaymotors.com</A>  , and you might just find yourself a good deal. I always check out those places to ind some good pictures. I won't be able to aford one for a long time though.  I could hardly afford my Fiero, lol.<BR>Good luck, maybe you'll find what you're looking for.||||reg||1
